# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
#
# .beads/ MUST stay ignored in the tracked .gitignore, not just in
# .git/info/exclude. The exclude file is machine-local and does not travel with a
# clone, so without this line a teammate who clones and runs any bd command would
# see .beads/ as untracked and could commit it. This repository is PUBLIC, and
# .beads/issues.jsonl here is a ~2 MB export of the whole Intent Solutions estate
# (1,207 issues under the bd_000-projects prefix), not just now-lms work.
.beads/
.dolt/
.beads-credential-key
# Teaching content lives in the private intent-solutions-io/intent-curriculum
# repo and must never be committed here (ADR 000-docs/008-AT-ADEC): this fork is
# public, and answer keys beside the courses that grade them is an
# assessment-integrity failure. A local checkout for seeding is fine — that is
# what CCA_CONTENT_DIR is for; this line stops it becoming a commit.
content/cca/
